; A parameter that nothing reads is STILL part of the interface.
;
; DCE keeps AIR_PARAM as a root for exactly this reason, and nothing
; verified that it did. Proven by injection: making is_root return false
; for AIR_PARAM deletes `unused` here and the ENTIRE regression suite --
; 74 assertions at the time, including a full verify of the result --
; stayed green. The verifier cannot catch it either: the parameter list
; is rebuilt from the surviving AIR_PARAM values, so "deleted a
; parameter" and "never had one" are indistinguishable afterwards.
;
; Dropping an argument is an ABI change. Every caller then passes its
; remaining arguments to the wrong slots, and nothing in the IR says so.
;
; a2 now captures each function's arity before DCE and compares after,
; reporting `DCE: arity kept : N changed`. This fixture is the one that
; makes that number move.
module /tmp/up.pie
func g entry=b1
  block b1
    %1 = mem.entry  [mem=entry:0<-0]
    %2 = param name=unused
    %3 = const.int ival=7  [range=7..7 w=64 kb=18446744073709551608/7]
    ret %3
  end
endfunc
